  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Alan Sugar is a British entrepreneur who built his fortune through Amstrad's affordable electronics and home computers. Raised on a Hackney council estate, he started trading with his own savings. He later built the Amsprop commercial-property portfolio and became widely known as the investor at the centre of television's The Apprentice.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 96,
